    "field": "Convection-permitting climate modeling",
    "problem": "Evaluations of promising convection-permitting models are limited, lacking an integrated interpretation of how cloud property deficiencies create biases in near-surface temperature and precipitation, particularly for regions with weak orographic forcing.",
    "method": "This paper comprehensively evaluates a convection-permitting climate model by comparing an 11-year simulation of precipitation, temperature, and cloud properties against various in-situ and satellite-based observations to assess its performance and identify remaining biases.",
    "task": "The task is to evaluate how well a convection-permitting climate model reproduces decadal statistics of precipitation, temperature, and cloud characteristics for a mid-latitude coastal region with little orographic forcing.",
